 "result": "Call order (this repo is `tessel`, a Flask-like framework):\n\n1. `Tessel.finalize_request` — `src/tessel/app.py:1021`. It is called after view dispatch (line 1019), and from the error handler (line 948). It calls `make_response` and then `finalize_reply`.\n2. `Tessel.finalize_reply` — `src/tessel/app.py:1394`. It runs the `after_request` functions, then writes the session if it isn't the null session (lines 1415–1416).\n3. `SessionInterface.is_null_session` — `src/tessel/sessions.py`. This is the guard on the write.\n4. `SignedCookieSessionInterface.persist_session` — `src/tessel/sessions.py:337`. This is where the cookie is written:\n   - It reads the cookie settings through the `get_cookie_*` helpers (`sessions.py:172–221`).\n   - `cookie_needs_write` (`sessions.py:233`) decides whether a write is needed at all.\n   - `make_signer` (`sessions.py:303`) builds the signer, and `.dumps(dict(session))` serializes and signs the data.\n   - `response.set_cookie(...)` (`sessions.py:374`) sets the cookie. If the session was modified to empty, it calls `response.delete_cookie` instead (line 356).\n\n`src/tessel/testing.py:177` has a similar path that calls `persist_session` directly.",
